          "name": "scan",
          "rules": [
            {
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Keep credential and personal-data content out of logs\n\n- Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change.\n- Remove the value from the log entry, or log a non-revealing fact (presence, length, match result, or a non-reversible identifier) instead.\n- Log an allowlist of fields rather than whole request bodies, queries, or header sets. Never log Authorization or Cookie header values.\n- If redaction is required, apply a verified redaction before the logger call or in the logger's configuration, and test that emitted lines no longer contain the value.\n- Do not send credentials in URL query strings; access logs, proxies, and browser history record URLs. Use a request body or header instead.\n\nIllustrative example (unverified):\n\n```typescript\n// Illustrative: log a fact about the credential, not the credential.\nconsole.info('login attempt', { username, passwordProvided: typeof password === 'string' \u0026\u0026 password.length \u003e 0 });\n```\n",
                "text": "Keep credential and personal-data content out of logs. Remediate established vulnerabilities and poor practice. For Review items, resolve the named evidence before deciding whether or how behavior needs to change. Remove the value from the log entry, or log a non-revealing fact (presence, length, match result, or a non-reversible identifier) instead. Log an allowlist of fields rather than whole request bodies, queries, or header sets. Never log Authorization or Cookie header values. If redaction is required, apply a verified redaction before the logger call or in the logger's configuration, and test that emitted lines no longer contain the value. Do not send credentials in URL query strings; access logs, proxies, and browser history record URLs. Use a request body or header instead."
              },
              "id": "scan/sensitive-data-logging",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
